WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:03.492
Unit eighteen. Sleep and Screens!

2
00:00:04.466 --> 00:00:08.692
Hello, everyone! I'm Nurse Bopha, your school nurse.

3
00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:12.186
Hi, Nurse Bopha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.236 --> 00:00:16.249
Today we learn about Sleep and Screens. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:20.434
Sleep. Say it with me. Sleep!

6
00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:27.433
Screen. Say it with me. Screen!

7
00:00:30.952 --> 00:00:34.419
Blue light. Say it with me. Blue light!

8
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.493
Bedtime. Say it with me. Bedtime!

9
00:00:44.973 --> 00:00:48.406
Brain. Say it with me. Brain!

10
00:00:51.906 --> 00:00:55.306
Mood. Say it with me. Mood!

11
00:00:58.805 --> 00:01:02.138
Phone. Say it with me. Phone!

12
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.193
Routine. Say it with me. Routine!

13
00:01:12.695 --> 00:01:21.843
Using a screen at bedtime can keep my brain awake. Blue light and exciting games make sleep harder. Keeping my phone out of the bedroom improves sleep and mood.

14
00:01:21.893 --> 00:01:23.085
I can do that too!

15
00:01:24.593 --> 00:01:29.723
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:29.773 --> 00:01:30.923
Blue light!

17
00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:37.127
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:37.177 --> 00:01:38.327
Phone!

19
00:01:39.126 --> 00:01:44.435
Did you know? Children aged 6–12 need about 9–12 hours of sleep each night!

20
00:01:44.485 --> 00:01:46.749
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:55.417
Think and answer. Where could you charge your phone at night?

22
00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:56.617
Great answer!

23
00:01:57.763 --> 00:02:02.650
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.294
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

